Subject: [PATCH] Preserve legacy premultiplied user-texture bytes on 4.2

The ProjectM-TV 4.1.7 loader at source 43023889 uses SOIL_LOAD_RGBA with
SOIL_FLAG_MULTIPLY_ALPHA. The 4.2 stbi upload previously skipped that step.
Preserve the exact integer (rgb * alpha + 128) >> 8 arithmetic, including
its opaque-channel rounding, before the existing RGBA upload. Alpha bytes
retain their decoded values. This is a TV migration compatibility repair.

Reference: historical vendor/SOIL2/SOIL2.c multiply-alpha loop, lines 1523-1527.
The frozen rand-tritex regression differs at all 480 RGB frames before this
step and matches the released-source baseline at all 480 frames in two
GLES 3.0 repeats with this isolated change. See the rebase evidence.

--- a/src/libprojectM/Renderer/TextureManager.cpp
+++ b/src/libprojectM/Renderer/TextureManager.cpp
@@ -274,1 +274,10 @@
+    // Preserve SOIL2 multiply-alpha pixel bytes used by the released TV engine.
+    auto* img = imageData.get();
+    for (int i = 0; i < 4 * width * height; i += 4)
+    {
+        img[i + 0] = (img[i + 0] * img[i + 3] + 128) >> 8;
+        img[i + 1] = (img[i + 1] * img[i + 3] + 128) >> 8;
+        img[i + 2] = (img[i + 2] * img[i + 3] + 128) >> 8;
+    }
+
     auto format = TextureFormatFromChannels(4);
